{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"lacelike-corked-tattler","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Restore the READ-ONLY S3-backed live **Jira Cloud** multi-project bridge\nrehearsal that was mistakenly discarded during the DC pivot. The direction was\nto pursue BOTH paths: (a) complete the Cloud testing achievable with the 2\navailable live projects (REB + DIG), AND (b) pursue Jira DC (sibling 368f) for\nfreely-created throwaway projects. Only (b) survived; this ticket restores (a).\n\n## Why (complements 368f, does not duplicate it)\n368f's DC harness is git/file-backed, uses low-volume throwaway projects, and\nnever touches S3. This path exercises the two dimensions 368f cannot: the **S3\nstore backend** and **real Cloud ticket volume/diversity** across 2 real\nprojects.\n\n## Hard constraint — READ-ONLY on Jira\nNO outbound writes to Jira Cloud. Do NOT run outbound `bridge_sync` create/update\nagainst Cloud. Only:\n- INBOUND reconcile (Cloud -> S3 ticket store), and\n- `bridge_preview` (dry-run; already proven read-only: Mode.DRY_RUN ->\n  MODE_CAPS=0 -> persist=False; sole write path `_apply_batch` gated on\n  `not is_dry_run and persist`).\nAll mutations confined to a THROWAWAY S3 ticket store (bucket\n`rebar-rehearsal-368f-896586841071`, or a fresh throwaway prefix/bucket).\n\n## Avoid the prior failure\nThe deleted harness (git `ab9c452dd3`, `tests/external/live_multi_project/`)\nseeded NON-EXISTENT project keys (REBEMPTY/REBGHOST); real Jira JQL parse-errors\non an absent key and the inbound fetcher fails closed (correct product\nbehaviour). Map ONLY real, reachable projects (REB, DIG). If \"unknown project\"\nis tested at all, assert its true fail-closed outcome — never expect an inbound\nfetch of an absent key to succeed.\n\n## What to validate (many-to-many over S3, read-only)\n1. One S3-backed store maps BOTH REB and DIG (many projects -> one store).\n2. Inbound reconcile pulls real tickets from BOTH projects into the S3 store\n   with correct per-project resolution/attribution (bridge_project), at real\n   volume/diversity.\n3. `bridge_preview` over the multi-project mapping is read-only and scoped\n   correctly per project (no cross-project contamination).\n4. The S3 store backend round-trips (git-remote-s3 push/clone) with the mapping\n   intact.\n5. ZERO Jira mutations (assert via read-only before/after counts and/or by never\n   invoking outbound sync; enforce structurally).\n\n## Infra (all available)\nAWS profile `frontier`, us-east-1; encrypted bucket\n`rebar-rehearsal-368f-896586841071` (exists) or a fresh throwaway prefix;\n`git-remote-s3` installed in `.venv`; Jira Cloud creds JIRA_URL/JIRA_USER/\nJIRA_API_TOKEN (local + GitHub secrets); `acli` read-only.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. A NEW live test suite exercises the read-only S3+Cloud scenarios above and is\n   wired into CI (a dedicated job or the external lane), gated by\n   REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL + Cloud/AWS creds, with the read-only invariant enforced\n   structurally (the suite cannot invoke outbound Jira sync).\n2. An ACTUAL green live run against REB + DIG demonstrates: both projects\n   fetched into one S3 store, correct per-project resolution, read-only preview\n   scoping, S3 round-trip, and ZERO Jira writes.\n3. The throwaway S3 test store is cleaned up after the run.","id":"5014-d0c6-5bbe-47fb","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Read-only S3-backed live Jira Cloud multi-project rehearsal (REB + DIG)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786763238956278001,"uuid":"d71a6c61-8c03-4e0e-b1e8-01d4066d571b"}